smartinit.v4.2.1

NAM Smartinit changes associated with Dell Transition (see docs/README for more details on changes)

* used compath.py for definitions of COM_SREF and COM_IN

* created new modulefile, changed mpirun command, and updated the build scripts for use on the Dell

* removed hard-wired link to /com/date/t${cyc}z file

* fixed bug in subroutine rdgrib

* SMARTPRECIP needed many changes to run on the Dell:  GRIB2 Grid Definition Template and Data Representation Template arrays
  needed to be redefined before writing the total accumulated precipitation and snow depths to the GRIB2 file.
  In addition, binary scaling needed to be forced to adequate precision (-4) and Subroutine Getbit needed to be called
  to calculate nbits (number of bits needed for packing).

#===============================================================================
 IMPLEMENTATION INSTRUCTIONS 
#===============================================================================

1.  git clone -b RB-v4.2.1 ssh://${USER}@vlab.ncep.noaa.gov:29418/EMC_smartinit smartinit.v4.2.1

    to set up and run on the Dell.

2.  Copy fixed files to the fix directory

    cp -r /gpfs/dell2/emc/modeling/noscrub/Annette.Gibbs/emc-binaries/smartinit/fix smartinit.v4.2.1

2.  Build sorc codes smartinit_g2.fd, smartprecip_g2.fd
       
	The modulefile used for the build is in modulefiles/SMARTINIT/v4.2.1.  Copy it to a location from which it can
	be loaded (/nwprod2/modulefiles/SMARTINIT or something similar). 

	In the smartinit sorc directory "smartinit.v4.2.1/sorc" type
		./build_smartinit_all.sh
	to compile the codes sequentially.  All executables will be copied over to the smartinit "exec" directory.

4.  Use ...docs/smartinit.ver file if desired to set
      model_ver=v4.2.1  parameter

